        "book": "2 Samuel",
        "chapter": 19,
        "verse": 33
      },
      {
        "text": "And Barzillai said unto the king, How long have I to live, that I should go up with the king unto Jerusalem?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 34,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Samuel 19:34",
        "book": "2 Samuel",
        "chapter": 19,
        "verse": 34
      },
      {
        "text": "I am this day fourscore years old: and can I discern between good and evil? can thy servant taste what I eat or what I drink? can I hear any more the voice of singing men and singing women? wherefore then should thy servant be yet a burden unto my lord the king?",
        "footNotes": [],
